OL,3,GNEWSAFarmer fears onion shortage unless
OL,4,Aretailers adapt
OL,5,
OL,6,FA farmer said he feared there would be
OL,7,Fshortages of onions this Christmas if
OL,8,Fsupermarkets did not adjust their
OL,9,Frequirements, with the severe heat and
OL,10,Fdrought creating smaller vegetables.
OL,12,FAndrew Long, who farms in Suffolk, has
OL,13,Fbeen forced to harvest his onions three
OL,14,Fweeks earlier than usual due to the
OL,15,Fweather conditions.
OL,17,FHe said onions were required to be
OL,18,Fabout 60-80mm (2.4-3.1in) in diameter
OL,19,Ffor the supermarkets, but much of his
OL,20,Fcrop has only measured 40-60mm
OL,21,F(1.6-2.4in).
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
